TEXT 32 32 Left 3 ;#327 Wilson PNP current mirror: ideal output-voltage sweep experiment
TEXT 32 96 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2IbWvq7Abv4
TEXT 32 144 Left 2 ;The same Wilson mirror, with Q3's collector voltage swept directly. The nearly flat current shows the much higher output resistance that Q3's feedback provides.
TEXT 32 832 Left 2 ;Vload replaces Alan's ammeter and adjustable load in this separate experiment. Vload sets Q3's collector voltage; I(Vload) is the output current.
TEXT 32 880 Left 2 !.dc Vload 0 11 0.1
TEXT 32 912 Left 2 !.meas dc I_AT_0V FIND I(Vload) AT=0
TEXT 32 944 Left 2 !.meas dc I_AT_5V FIND I(Vload) AT=5
TEXT 32 976 Left 2 !.meas dc ROUT_OHMS PARAM 5/(I_AT_0V-I_AT_5V)
